  "rules": "A row maps a benchmark to one registry target. With version null it covers the stem and stem-<suffix> (longest stem, then exact id wins); otherwise it covers its exact id only. counted, or benchmark when absent, is the coverage key: versions and re-measurers count once within a class; slices never add coverage. metric null does not pool different metrics. direct gives coverage; proxy is a marked substitute and never coverage; facet names a facet; unmapped has no target. A direct row may carry subsetOf (its own key measures a subset of that benchmark) and substituteIn (classes where it is only a marked substitute). New class-table rows name PROTO-DEC-0321 item 7, a basis and checks []; only the closed set held by the registry qualifies; a later owner decision is cited in the basis. Legacy rows retain their decision or two independent checks. Quarantine, crosswalk labels, removed and unknown IDs are never targets. Class disagreements and partial fits are recorded in the source repository.",
